{"id": "EUVD-2026-101041", "enisaUuid": "a68d298d-0b18-3a77-8ba4-34a38e6a2e43", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: fix tx_handle bounds off-by-one\n\nValid indices into txq->urbd0s/tfds/bufs are 0..txq->count-1, so\ntfd_index == txq->count is already out of range. Change the guard in\nbtintel_pcie_msix_tx_handle() from '> txq->count' to '>= txq->count'.\n\nThis issue was reported by Claude Mythos.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:25:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72bbd7c815ef92399b7b109977ae4669ce22ee6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/932a87444107e6724d808082676bba5c915c98ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a641201a9b4d69ee8a7ef35f7aa597dddee6b9ee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3dd1b41f96aad08444be1b7626c89de2b9f2abd4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j4c2-pp7j-2j5f", "CVE-2026-98392"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05a78920-e371-32de-99d1-47091229ae73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "06eddf8f-ae91-3646-a402-e5f523ac0cc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <72bbd7c815ef92399b7b109977ae4669ce22ee6e"}, {"id": "2545f683-a945-3ae3-a47e-018825dc5d7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <3dd1b41f96aad08444be1b7626c89de2b9f2abd4"}, {"id": "5beb8d53-e0e3-3848-b103-3ae559aac3fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "6c8b2514-c24b-30d2-9ccb-23d0bfa39fdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "7685f5ed-6804-3914-9504-f8dc1a3f54cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": 